$$  
A function $ f $ is **odd** if it satisfies:  
$$
f(-x) = -f(x) \quad \text{for all } x \in \mathbb{R}
$$

### Step 2: Combine the conditions  
If a function is **both even and odd**, then it must satisfy both conditions simultaneously. That is:  
$$
f(-x) = f(x) \quad \text{and} \quad f(-x) = -f(x)
$$  
This means:  
$$
f(x) = -f(x)
$$  
for all $ x \in \mathbb{R} $.

