$$
f(x) = -f(x) \Rightarrow f(x) + f(x) = 0 \Rightarrow 2f(x) = 0 \Rightarrow f(x) = 0
$$  
This tells us that the only function that satisfies this condition is the **zero function**, defined by:  
$$
f(x) = 0 \quad \text{for all } x \in \mathbb{R}
$$

